    {
      "id": "Y0ef2KRuAIFXYa2SnhAlH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 136.6952776995289,
      "y": 1050.3756691633785,
      "width": 1475.47900390625,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1697891984,
      "version": 1286,
      "versionNonce": 188460176,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783483490235,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core Entities\n- Events\n- Users\n- Performers\n- Venues\n- Tickets\n- Bookings\n\nNote\nEvent stores actual info about event like date, description, performer, venue\nPerformers could be an individual or a group its description and their details, link to their socials\nVenues stores physical location lat long of the place, a seat map could be json or a separate table, capacity\nTicket stores specifics for each event and a specific venue, uses venue seat map and create tickets for each seat of the venue\neach ticket stores the price for the seat, its number, its status(available|booked)\nBooking records the details of user's purchased tickets, stores userId, ticketId, total price, booking status, payment details\nNow Its good to have a separate table for booking and not club it with tickets as when user purchases multiple tickets in one txn, we can\ngroup them under a single order with shared payment status and total price rather than editing all the rows for tickets with user and payment details\nClean and avoids duplication.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Core Entities\n- Events\n- Users\n- Performers\n- Venues\n- Tickets\n- Bookings\n\nNote\nEvent stores actual info about event like date, description, performer, venue\nPerformers could be an individual or a group its description and their details, link to their socials\nVenues stores physical location lat long of the place, a seat map could be json or a separate table, capacity\nTicket stores specifics for each event and a specific venue, uses venue seat map and create tickets for each seat of the venue\neach ticket stores the price for the seat, its number, its status(available|booked)\nBooking records the details of user's purchased tickets, stores userId, ticketId, total price, booking status, payment details\nNow Its good to have a separate table for booking and not club it with tickets as when user purchases multiple tickets in one txn, we can\ngroup them under a single order with shared payment status and total price rather than editing all the rows for tickets with user and payment details\nClean and avoids duplication.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hDFHEKBJQjxJQBcr7aUd8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 149.5478863728588,
      "y": 1597.7978011302087,
      "width": 1343.93896484375,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 171063920,
      "version": 670,
      "versionNonce": 1623478384,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783486186887,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "APIs\n\n// viewing an event\nGET /events/:eventId  -> Event & Venue & Performer & Ticket[]\n- tickets are to render the seat map on the client\n\n\n// searching the events\nGET /events/search?keyword={keyword}&start={start_date}&end={end_date}&pageSize={page_size}&page={page_number} --> Event[]\n- location(lat&long) could also be added to filter events using venues based on requested location, using ES geohashing search\n\n\n// booking a ticket\nPOST /bookings/:eventId -> bookingId\n{\n    \"ticketIds\": string[],\n    \"paymentDetails\": ...\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "APIs\n\n// viewing an event\nGET /events/:eventId  -> Event & Venue & Performer & Ticket[]\n- tickets are to render the seat map on the client\n\n\n// searching the events\nGET /events/search?keyword={keyword}&start={start_date}&end={end_date}&pageSize={page_size}&page={page_number} --> Event[]\n- location(lat&long) could also be added to filter events using venues based on requested location, using ES geohashing search\n\n\n// booking a ticket\nPOST /bookings/:eventId -> bookingId\n{\n    \"ticketIds\": string[],\n    \"paymentDetails\": ...\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
