      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783487449353,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- This has lot of potential issues but at the very least it satisfies all our functional requirements.\n- Notice, how multiple services share the same DB, the \"database per service\" rule gets repeated a lot but its not necessary.\n Here a shared DB is the right call because the data is tightly coupled, we need ACID txns for booking, and splitting DB will add complexities \n with no real benefits. Explain this trade-off in interviews.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- This has lot of potential issues but at the very least it satisfies all our functional requirements.\n- Notice, how multiple services share the same DB, the \"database per service\" rule gets repeated a lot but its not necessary.\n Here a shared DB is the right call because the data is tightly coupled, we need ACID txns for booking, and splitting DB will add complexities \n with no real benefits. Explain this trade-off in interviews.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jOjNziLWAtP3nAG29-dzd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2014.3677957628297,
      "y": 641.5425219116585,
      "width": 150.99443535484164,
